I tested everything against 3.0 branch (on yesterday's git) - I am pretty sure that the issue was there.

@t8m well, I did that mistake in the beginning :) But now I have Debian without any openssl3 files (purged everything) and I use just "make install" from the devel git (it only requires Debianish paths for Config) - so it is loading the devel-compiled legacy.so. I'll try strace.

@mbroz i'm not sure what you mean.  looking back over this issue, an attempt was made to fix it, at which point the attempt was abandoned as not being a good approach, and then the issue sat uncommented for almost 3 years.  That suggests to me that this is in fact not at all a high priority to fix.

As such, I don't forsee openssl expending resources to address this in the near future, unless something changes to identify it as a high priority (a large community of people experiencing the issue, a production regression, etc).

Barring that, a PR is always welcome.  If you are interested in fixing it, I'm happy to assign this to you as a community issue if you like.
